# No invites until asked

Do **not** send emails, auth invites, password resets, or magic links unless the user explicitly says to (e.g. “invite”, “send the invite”, “email them”).

- Do not call `inviteUserByEmail`, `resetPasswordForEmail`, or similar
- Creating a seat, linking a name, or syncing the allocation matrix is **not** permission to provision a login
- If an account is needed later, wait for an explicit ask
- When invites **are** sent, use `inviteUserByEmailWithArchive`, which sends `information@seamun.com` a separate archive copy with the set-password links removed (never a BCC). Do not call `inviteUserByEmail` directly.
